# H1: hand the cards back to production. This is the LAST job of the window and it runs even when any earlier job failed, stalled or hung (a hang can leave all four
# cards wedged with production down): the status of every board, the all-four reset, the fabric re-measure (the four-card probe: the ring, the link count and the
# collectives timed; it must pass before production serves), then the node agent starts again and waits for its container to answer /v1/models. The agent serves the rig
# daemon's local :latest, which this window did NOT move, so the placement the owner's /deploy then makes is TODAY'S PRODUCTION RECIPE (profile c2-packed-tp4: audits off,
# the pinned sampler in the verify trace).
# NEVER place a gate arm or this window's image: not the V5 twins, not the audited arm, not any gate-only profile.
# AN OWNER /deploy IS STILL NEEDED, always, to place today's production recipe or anything new: this job starts the agent with nothing placed; it never includes a deploy,
# a :latest retag or a placement call. If the fabric re-measure fails the job stops before agentstart: production stays down until a board is healed.
# Pass: all four boards enumerate after the reset, the fabric probe passes, /v1/models answers Qwen/Qwen3.8-27B:tt and a chat completes, and the engine log shows profile
# c2-packed-tp4 with the audits off and QWEN_FAST_PACKED_SAMPLER_IN_TRACE=1.
# Duration (estimate): reset 1-3 min, fabric probe 5-10 min, agent start and model load 10-15 min: 25 min.
# A committed TEMPLATE of .github/c2-serving-job.env for the tp4/v5split window (scripts/ci/c2_serving_job.py parses it): copy it over
# .github/c2-serving-job.env on a throwaway commit of tp4/v5split and push a tag experiment/c2-serving-vN (the tag numbers are the driver's, on the
# allowlist). Nothing here names a rig, a card, a host or a registry: the cards are resolved at run time. The jobs are templates only: no tag is
# pushed from this branch.
# TWO IMAGES: C2_IMAGE_TAG=tp4-v5split-1 (a PLACEHOLDER the driver substitutes) is the build the single-card byte gate runs in (the gate mounts this
# checkout's scripts, so any current C2 image carries the runtime it needs); C2_IMAGE_TAG=tp4-v5split-2 is the build of the commit that adds the
# qualified sha256 triple (gdn_seq_block_split.QUALIFIED), which the four-card jobs serve. A reused tag is skipped by the build step.
C2_CARDS=quad
C2_ACTIONS=status reset fabric agentstart
C2_IMAGE_TAG=tp4-v5split-2
